'' 'virtual' needs a vtable, and only a type that extends OBJECT has one; 'abstract'
'' implies virtual and is the same refusal. An abstract method has no body. And
'' 'operator new' and its siblings are implicitly STATIC, so neither modifier fits them.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/virtual-needs-object.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' GOLDEN: expected/virtual-needs-object.out
